## Give movement a job

An entrance can show where a new section begins. A transition can connect two ideas. Motion is most useful when it helps someone understand the page.

## Let the reader keep control

Avoid trapping the wheel or forcing horizontal movement through a long sequence. The page should still be readable when scripts fail or when someone prefers reduced motion.

## Start quietly

Try a short fade and a small movement before adding a more elaborate effect. Test a narrow screen, keyboard navigation and a return to the page halfway down.

